  "details": "What it says on the tin. Cloth physics. Love em or hate em, they're there, and fairly useful in spots. But they do not properly reflect in mirrors, they render, but their state and physics render entirely differently, as if they were an entirely different object. Which makes it obviously worse when compounded with the animation reflection problem, as having a dedicated gesture/emote that resets the cloth, does NOT reflect in the mirror, resulting in de synced cloth states between the mirror and actuality.\n\nMakes taking selfies virtually impossible when your cloth physics are messed up in the mirror.",
